    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The sides of a rectangular table are 150 cm and 360 cm. What is the length of the diagonal?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$390\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "The diagonal divides the rectangle into two right-angled triangles. Let $d$ be the length of the diagonal in centimetres. By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2&=150^2+360^2\\\\d^2&=22500+129600\\\\d^2&=152100\\\\d&=\\sqrt{152100}\\\\d&=390.\\end{align*}$$\nThe diagonal is $390\\text{ cm}$ long.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
